# Spectral Gap Rigidity for Abstract Hodge Laplacians

A self-contained, `sorry`-free local-to-global theory for abstract Hodge Laplacians
and its consequences for spectral-gap message passing.  The architecture mirrors the
sheaf-theoretic playbook: a **stalk-level** rigidity fact is proved first, glued into
a **global** harmonicity criterion, made **functorial** under coarse-graining, and
finally turned into **quantitative dynamics**.

The conceptual spine is a single pointwise identity,
`psd_operator_inner_self_eq_zero`: for a symmetric positive–semidefinite operator,
the *scalar* energy equation `⟪x, L x⟫ = 0` forces the *vector* equation `L x = 0`.
This is the algebraic analogue of "a harmonic form with zero energy is zero," and it
is proved purely algebraically via the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality for the
positive–semidefinite bilinear form `B(x,y) = ⟪x, L y⟫` — **no spectral theorem and
no finite-dimensionality is used**.

From this stalk fact we obtain, by `inner_add_right` bookkeeping alone:

* `harmonic_iff` — the Hodge harmonicity criterion: a cochain is globally harmonic
  (`Δ x = 0`) iff it is locally closed and coclosed (`up x = 0 ∧ down x = 0`).  This
  is the algebraic heart of `ker Δ ≅ H*`, the local-to-global gluing of cohomology.
* `harmonic_pushforward` — cohomology is functorial under any intertwiner.
* `gap_transfer_isometry` — an isometric intertwiner transfers the spectral gap
  exactly (coarse-graining an expander into an isometric model preserves the gap).
* `gap_implies_vanishing` — a positive spectral gap kills all harmonics (an expander
  has no nontrivial cohomology).

The message-passing engine (`mpStep`, `mpStep_contraction`,
`mpStep_iterate_contraction`, `gap_mpStep_converges`, `gap_optimal_mpStep_converges`)
then drives every signal to the trivial cohomology at the spectral rate `1 - μ/λ`,
with the spectral step `α = 1/λ` optimal (`contraction_factor_optimal`).

## Main results

* `psd_operator_inner_self_eq_zero` — stalk rigidity of the energy form.
* `hodgeLaplacian_symm`, `hodgeLaplacian_psd` — `Δ = up + down` is symmetric PSD.
* `harmonic_iff` — global harmonic ⇔ local closed + coclosed.
* `harmonic_pushforward` — functoriality of cohomology under intertwiners.
* `gap_transfer_isometry` — isometric intertwiners transfer the spectral gap.
* `gap_implies_vanishing` — positive gap ⇒ trivial harmonic space.
* `mpStep_apply`, `mpStep_harmonic_fixed`, `mpStep_iterate_harmonic_fixed` — the
  message-passing layer and exact transport of harmonics.
* `mpStep_contraction`, `mpStep_iterate_contraction`, `gap_mpStep_converges` —
  per-layer and geometric energy contraction, convergence to tolerance.
* `contraction_factor_optimal`, `contraction_factor_at_optimal`,
  `gap_optimal_mpStep_converges` — the spectral step `α = 1/λ` is optimal with rate
  `1 - μ/λ`, and deep optimal message passing collapses every signal.

